name: pbr-repos-need-git-for-version
description: OpenStack pbr-based repos (stevedore etc.) fail pip install unless git is installed and /testbed is marked safe
metadata:
  type: project
---

In setupbench minimal Ubuntu 22.04 environments, `pip install -e /testbed` on pbr-based OpenStack repos fails with "Versioning for this project requires either an sdist tarball, or access to an upstream git repository".

**Why:** pbr derives the package version from git metadata at build time; the base image has no `git` binary, and even after installing it, git refuses the repo owned by uid 1000 ("dubious ownership").

**How to apply:** `apt-get install -y git` then `git config --global --add safe.directory /testbed` before any pip install of the repo. Verified working for openstack/stevedore (2026-09-10).
